  "details": "<p>The basilica today houses the Church of the Redeemer. It is the largest extant hall from antiquity measuring 67 x 26.05 m, with a height of 33 m. The building was substantially damaged during World War II and restored afterwards.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Aula Palatina is a Roman Imperial Basilica of the emperor Constantine (German: Konstantinbasilika) located at Trier, Germany. It was built ca. A.D. 310 as part of a Roman palace complex.",
